  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: in S Etruria</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The Subertani were an ancient people of South Etruria. Pliny the Elder places them in Regio VII. The center of Forum Subertanum is mentioned in Livy's account of 211 B.C. Lugli suggests it is possible that their territory was located in the province of Viterbo.",
